course: dictionary
lesson: 8605
title: Reading a face in words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scowl is a frown that shows anger or bad temper. You can see it on a face without anyone saying a word, so writers use it to show feelings. «The giant scowled down at Jack» tells you the giant is cross, even though he says nothing.
explain: Scowl can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it is something you do: «Maddie scowls». As a noun it is something you have: a scowl on your face. Look out for phrases like scowl at, a deep scowl and with a scowl.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Maddie scowls — and the next day she says sorry to Chloe.» The words «the next day» are a clue: a scowl can pass, so it shows how someone feels in that moment, not always how they will feel for ever.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «The giant frowned angrily down at Jack» still makes sense, so frown in an angry way is a good meaning for scowl. In drama lessons, actors practise scowls and smiles to show feelings with their faces.
fact: To scowl means to frown in an angry or bad-tempered way.
fact: A scowl is an angry frown on someone's face.
fact: Scowl is a verb (scowl, scowls, scowled, scowling) and a noun (a scowl, scowls).
fact: «Scowl at» means to look at someone with an angry frown.
fact: A scowl can show that someone is cross, grumpy or jealous, even without any words.
exercise: «The giant scowled down at Jack.» What does scowled mean? | Yawned sleepily | Smiled warmly | *Frowned angrily | Laughed loudly
exercise: «Maddie gave a deep scowl.» What is a scowl here? | A kind hug | A loud song | A jump over a puddle | *An angry frown on her face
exercise: Which clue in «Maddie scowls — and the next day she says sorry to Chloe.» shows the scowl did not last long? | scowls | Chloe | Maddie | *the next day
test: «She scowled at the rain and stayed indoors.» What does scowled mean here? | Shouted for help | Smiled at the rain | Danced in the rain | *Frowned in a bad-tempered way
test: Which sentence uses scowl as a noun? | Scowling, he left the room. | He scowled at the door. | They scowled together. | *She had a scowl on her face.
exam: «The teacher gave Sam a scowl when he ran in.» What does the scowl show? | Surprise at a present | Tiredness after a long day | *Anger or bad temper | Happiness and joy
